{# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   THE UPLOAD COMPONENT — one component, two presentations, one behaviour.

   Every place a file enters the product wears one of these. Rendered by
   `render_upload(target, presentation, attrs)`; its behaviour is
   assets/controllers/upload_controller.js; its vocabulary is the SHELL's
   `.upl-*`, shipped in shell.css ahead of this component for exactly this
   reason — a file enters through more than one door, so the box belongs to the
   frame rather than to whichever module needed it first. Nothing here defines a
   class, a token or an inline style.

   WHAT IS SERVER-RENDERED AND WHAT IS NOT. Only the IDLE state is markup: the
   waiting zone, or the one add tile. Every other state — the queue, the
   progress, the refusal, the finished chip, the removal question — is drawn by
   the controller, because each of them is about a file that did not exist when
   the page was rendered. The idle state is snapshotted on connect and restored,
   so its wording lives in one place and is the template's.

   THE PICKER IS NOT HERE, DELIBERATELY. An `<input type="file">` cannot sit
   inside the add tile (a `<button>` may not contain form controls) and must not
   sit beside it (it would take a cell of the grid). The controller creates it,
   which also means this template never ships a control that does nothing.

   THE TILE'S SIBLINGS ARE THE GRID'S. In the tile presentation this element is
   ONE CELL of the module's own evidence grid, and the tiles the controller draws
   while a file is in flight are inserted beside it, in that same grid — which is
   why `.upl-tile` states its box once and no state changes its size or radius.
   ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}

{%- set kinds = constraints.extensions|join(' · ') -%}
{%- set sizeLabel = constraints.maxBytes|storage_bytes -%}

{#- Everything the controller was told, spelled from Uhifadhi\Storage\Upload\UploadDom
    so the same string appears in the PHP, in this template and in the asset.
    UploadSeamTest is what keeps the three the same. -#}
{%- set wiring -%}
    data-controller="uhifadhi--storage-module--upload"
    data-upl-root
    data-upl-target="{{ target }}"
    data-upl-token="{{ token }}"
    data-upl-upload-url="{{ uploadUrl }}"
    data-upl-remove-url="{{ removeUrl }}"
    data-upl-accept="{{ constraints.accept }}"
    data-upl-max-files="{{ constraints.maxFiles }}"
    data-upl-presentation="{{ presentation }}"
    {%- if attrs.input is defined %} data-upl-input-name="{{ attrs.input }}"{% endif -%}
    {%- for name, value in attrs|filter((value, name) => name not in ['input', 'label']) %} {{ name }}="{{ value }}"{% endfor -%}
{%- endset -%}

{% if presentation == 'tile' %}
    {#- ONE CELL OF AN EVIDENCE GRID. Dashed, the plus, the label — and it is a
        real <button>, so the keyboard reaches it without a line of ours. -#}
    <button type="button" class="upl-tile idle" {{ wiring }}>
        {{ ux_icon('storage:plus', {width: 15, height: 15}) }}
        <span class="lbl">{{ attrs.label|default('Add evidence') }}</span>
    </button>
{% else %}
    {#- RECEIVING THE FILE IS THE STEP, so the component takes the width it needs
        and states its own rules. -#}
    <div class="upl-zone" {{ wiring }}>
        {{ ux_icon('storage:upload', {width: 26, height: 26}) }}
        <span class="lead" data-upl-lead>{{ attrs.label|default('Drop files here, or') }}
            <a href="#" data-upl-browse>browse</a></span>
        {#- The queue. Empty and hidden until there is a file in it: an empty box
            with a border would be a state the design does not have. -#}
        <div class="upl-list" data-upl-list hidden></div>
        {#- THE RULE, STATED UP FRONT. The design is explicit that the allowed
            kinds and the size limit are read here and never discovered by being
            refused — so both figures come from the very constraints the endpoint
            enforces, and neither is typed. -#}
        <span class="upl-kinds">{{ kinds }} &nbsp;·&nbsp; up to {{ sizeLabel }} each · {{ constraints.maxFiles }} files at a time</span>
    </div>
{% endif %}
